# "Creatures target player controls can't block this turn" is a rule about the player until end of turn (CR 509.1b, 611.2c), not a
# list of the creatures there were: Bot2 flashes Snapcaster Mage into play AFTER Scarlett's trigger has resolved (Island and
# Mox Sapphire), and it still cannot block her. The refusal here names a legal-looking block that the engine never even
# asks about (no block is possible at all, so no question comes); the control, with Scarlett aimed at her own controller, lets
# the same Snapcaster block (headliner-scarlett-snapcaster-flashed-in-blocks-when-she-targets-her-controller).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Headliner Scarlett
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Snapcaster Mage
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Headliner Scarlett.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Snapcaster Mage.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Headliner Scarlett)
! Bot2.Block(Snapcaster Mage > Headliner Scarlett)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield.Snapcaster Mage.Damage = 0
